  "limitations": [
    "Installer G (2020) and UK user E (2021) are separately labelled baselines; this is not LightSYS+ or a claim about current firmware.",
    "The seven guided lessons cover selected supported routes. Free exploration exposes the larger sourced tree, with explicit reference-only conditional hardware branches.",
    "UK user and installer operations use scroll navigation because their source tables do not publish exact numeric shortcuts.",
    "One By One zone programming, output programming, RF/device enrolment, firmware, reset/anticode and remote communications are reference-only.",
    "The source requires 0 then OK to save installer changes. Only the free emulator models the demo tamper exit gate.",
    "The basic lesson engine simplifies walk-test result text and resistance/voltage views; the free emulator implements the distinct source functions."
  ],
